      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_c2aec491",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "audience description",
      "description": "The target community is individuals who are familiar with or interested in debates surrounding religious freedom, legal rights of Muslim women, and Islamophobia. The meme is designed for an audience that understands the legal context of niqab inspections and may be engaged in discussions about religious expression versus state authority. It likely appeals to those who are politically or socially aware of issues related to Western values, gender equality, and civil liberties, particularly in contexts where such legal boundaries are contested. The visual framing and text suggest the audience is expected to interpret the image as a commentary on legal restrictions, potentially reinforcing or challenging existing stereotypes about Muslim women and their attire.",
